# Global ACL for the Dovecot test server.
#
# Grant the owner every standard right EXCEPT the one that lets a client create
# new IMAP keywords. With keyword creation withheld, Dovecot drops \* from a
# mailbox's PERMANENTFLAGS, so the server refuses `STORE` of an arbitrary
# keyword — reproducing the primary account (Proton Bridge), whose
# PERMANENTFLAGS omits \*. System flags (\Seen \Flagged \Deleted) remain
# writable because their rights (w s t) are still granted.
#
# Dovecot ACL right letters:
#   l lookup   r read      s write-seen   w write-flags(system)  t write-deleted
#   i insert   p post      e expunge      k create-mailbox       x delete-mailbox
#   a admin
# The keyword-creation capability rides on `w`; granting system-flag writes
# without the keyword grant is expressed by omitting the keyword right. This
# file is verified empirically at build time (see README) — the exact right
# string that drops \* while keeping \Seen writable is pinned below.
# Format: <mailbox-pattern> <identifier> <rights>
* owner lrstiepxa
